Why, climb batch 36. Not a new rule: three failures that the batch fixed. The list said that against the one library a compiled program fails at a call of a varargs declaration and at a reduction over a range, since a class fails to load (rows 1091 and 1099), and at = and < of two strings and = of two booleans (row 994). Climb batch 36 fixed all three in the code generator: each class now holds a method once by its name and descriptor, and the class of a generic function is named with its package. So those three bullets are gone, and a one-library run test can now hold these constructs. The paragraph’s first sentence, the list’s other three bullets and the sentence after the list stay. The batch found two more failures of a compiled program against the one library (rows 1137 and 1138). The skill writer added no bullet for them: by the curator’s decision P-180, a defect is fixed, not taught, and the coordinator plans their fixes. The cold read found nothing to fix here.

